# Violin Partita No. 1 in B minor, BWV 1002: Tempo di Borea (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a bourree in cut time, stately rather than skipping: the
# theme opens with full chords on the beat, and later runs in eighths
# drive to the high E. Two beats to the bar, firm and proud.
#
# Time signature: 2/2 with a quarter-note upbeat, 68 bars (A 1-20,
# B 21-68, each half entered on an upbeat). Mutopia file violin-6.mid
# is the seventh score of the partita (Allemanda, Double, Corrente,
# Double, Sarabande, Double, Tempo di Borea, Double): verified against
# 7.ly, the Tempo di Borea (6.ly is the Sarabande's Double, in 9/8; the
# MIDI is 2/2 and starts with the Borea's F sharp upbeat and B minor
# chords). Both halves repeat; the MIDI plays each once, so play writes
# them out.
#
# Range: G3 to E6, no notes lifted. Four-note chords (bars 1, 65) keep
# three notes.
#
# Tempo: half = 66, 136 bars with repeats, about 4:10. Unattributed
# track times found: 2:02 (an eMusic listing, likely without repeats:
# half about 67) and 3:59 (ototoy, likely with repeats: about 68). I
# could not confirm Szeryng's, Milstein's or Podger's timings. 66 is my
# judgment from those: weighty enough for the chords, still a dance.
#
# Structure (score bars, from 7.ly):
#   A  1-4    B minor, the chordal theme.
#      5-10   Toward D major, eighth-note answers.
#      11-17  Two-voice writing over a stepwise bass.
#      18-20  Eighth run and cadence in D major.
#   B  21-28  D major chords, to E minor (28).
#      29-38  F sharp minor, cadence (38).
#      39-44  Falling sequence with high answering notes.
#      45-53  Running eighths up to the high E (48), cadence (53-54).
#      55-64  Neapolitan C natural (56), runs, long held G (62).
#      65-68  The opening theme returns, B minor cadence.
#
# Bars as performed (play): A 0.75-20.75, A repeat 20.75-40.75,
# B 40.75-88.75 (score x = x+20), B repeat 88.75-136.75 (score x = x+68).

pickup 4
tempo 66 2

play 0.75-20.75 0.75-20.75 20.75-68.75 20.75-68.75

dyn 1 f              # A first time
dyn 20.75 mp         # A repeat, an echo
dyn 40.75 f          # B first time
dyn 59 mf            # score 39: the falling sequence
dyn 65 f             # score 45: the running eighths to the high E
dyn 88.75 mp         # B repeat, an echo
dyn 133 f            # score 65: the theme returns, full to the end

rit 2 0.8            # the final cadence
